RDMA-Tutorial example 2 (RC RDMA write) over RoCE, for rocm-ernic

Applied by ansible/playbooks/tutorial-tests.yml to
https://github.com/jcxue/RDMA-Tutorial at commit
f73736ed7a7d496f9acfc899e5d1997e791718ed. RDMA-Tutorial is licensed
under Apache-2.0, and so is this patch.

Upstream addresses the peer by InfiniBand LID. The emulated ionic NIC
is RoCE, which addresses it by GID, so this:

- Exchanges each side's IPv4-mapped GID along with its QP number, and
  connects the QP over a global route to the peer's.
- Uses the port's active MTU rather than a hardcoded 4096.
- Opens the device RDMA_TUTORIAL_DEV names, if it is set, rather than
  the first one.
- Lets TOT_NUM_OPS and NUM_WARMING_UP_OPS be set at build time: the
  defaults take tens of minutes over the emulated NIC.
- Links libibverbs, which the example calls directly, instead of
  librdmacm, which it never calls and which the guest image has no
  link-time library for.
- Includes <stdlib.h> for atoi(), which GCC 14 and later reject
  undeclared.
- Sets SO_REUSEADDR on the server's socket before binding it: every run
  uses the same port, and a rerun must not fail with EADDRINUSE while
  the last run's connection is still in TIME_WAIT.

